*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  Axes Control
*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  Module Description
*  - Clamping mode
*     The clamping mode can be (de)activated with M11/M10 or FN19. In FN19
*     you can define on which axes the M-functions have an effect. The first
*     numerical value is the identifier; its value has to be +99991 if the
*     clamping mode is inactive, and +99990 for an active clamping mode.
*     The second numerical value serves to transfer the axes in bit-encoded
*     form. This value is non-volatile and is maintained until FN19 is output
*     again.
*     e.g.:
*     FN 19: PLC =+99991 / +24 -> Clamping mode in axes 4 and 5 inactive
*
*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

#define /s    KL_distance_to_go                        K+4
#define /s    KL_handwheel_axis                        K+10
#define /s    KL_handwheel_axis_M118                   K+23
#define /s    KL_actual_value_fixed                    K+0
#define /s    KL_actual_value_released                 K+1
#define /s    KL_inactive                              K-1
#define /s    KL_runtime_from_MP                       K-1
#define /s    KL_servo_drive_release_axis_coded        K+2			  *;EUMACH BASIC 53
#define /s    KL_servo_drive_release_input_level       K+3			  *;EUMACH BASIC 53
#define /s    KL_mode_nominal_value_as_actual          K+0			  *;EUMACH BASIC 53
#define /s    KL_nominal_position                      K+1            *;EUMACH
#define /s    KL_torque_limitation                     K-1            *;EUMACH

#define /s    ML_servo_drives_releases                 M[16]
#define /c    ML_X_servo_drive_release                 M &ML_servo_drives_releases + 0
#define /c    ML_Y_servo_drive_release                 M &ML_servo_drives_releases + 1
